prefer 250-300. If your AC is decent and you're not Burdened, 400 or
more is overkill.

	The most I've ever ascended with was 610. That was a combination
of a long game (almost 200k turns) with an unusually large number of
extra healings kicking around the dungeon and the worst AC I've ever
ascended with - only -20. (Wishless, no magic markers in the entire
dungeon, and a distinct shortage of randomly generated enchant armor
scrolls.) Even with that, 600+ HP was not just excessive but
*ridiculously* excessive. I never even touched my full healing potions.
(My usual policy is to alchemize healing up to extra healing, bless and
quaff extra healing, and keep full healing for emergency use.)

	And nurse dancing I believe to be the devteam's method of
tricking otherwise indestructible characters into doing mind-bogglingly
stupid things like taking their armor off in the dungeon. I just kill
them. The meager hit points they provide aren't worth the risk that
getting nekkid for them entails. (If potions didn't increase max HP, I
might change my mind, but they do, so...)

